# React View Transitions

When implementing UI/page transitions in React, first use:

`~/.cursor/skills/react-view-transitions/SKILL.md`

Follow the implementation flow in `references/implementation.md` and reuse
animation recipes from `references/css-recipes.md`.

Apply the highest-value patterns that fit the feature:
- Shared element transitions with stable `name` identity.
- Suspense reveal transitions for loading to content swaps.
- List identity transitions via stable per-item `key`.
- Enter/exit transitions for appearing/disappearing UI.
- Route-level transitions for navigation context.

Prefer `default="none"` and explicitly opt into needed triggers to avoid
unintended global cross-fades.

When reporting changes, mention which transition patterns were applied.
